N5008 [temp.inst]/1: an alias declaration does not require a complete type,
so `using str = basic_str<char>;' (an alias TEMPLATE naming a class template
specialization whose argument is still incomplete) must not instantiate it.
The typedef branch of convert_non_template_declaration cleared
skip_typechecking_elaborate instead of restoring it when the alias template's
own declaration was converted underneath, so the outer resolver elaborated
the class (libstdc++ 11 pmr::string: "dropped 4 system-header declarations";
here: `a' never constructed, assertion 1 failed).
KNOWNBUG: fixing this by restoring skip_typechecking_elaborate after the
nested alias-template conversion (b79b14f901, reverted) broke
cpp20_ranges_pipe_invoke_drop: a specialization only named through an alias
template stays unelaborated and a later variadic constructor deduction from
an object of that type yields an empty pack.  That deduction-time
elaboration gap must be closed first (elaborate incomplete template
instances used as call-argument types; the guess_function_template_args
entry did not suffice -- the failing deduction runs elsewhere, from the
mem-initializer `__bound_args_(__bound_args...)' of __perfect_forward_impl).
